A||||15||BAM-BAM||The 87GT has been hit!!!!||||9||
Z||000000||BAM-BAM||11-29-2001||10:30 AM||||I have to say it's a dark day in all of Fierodom. My son was driving to the library at school when some nitwit chick tagged him from behind. She was driving a Ford Exploder. she hit him hard enough that it spun him through the stop sign. Now this where it gets shitty. The Police arrive and peruse the situation only to tell my son that there wasn't enough damage to write a citation. My son asked him (the policeman) if he might know where to get new parts for an 87GT, to which the guy said. "The local Chevy dealer carries all the parts he'll need. I don't think so!!!! <BR>  I guess there is some significant damage to the rear fascia and not sure about the tail lights yet. Everything was still covered with snow and mud. Oh yeah, did I mention that he is in Cedar City Utah!!! So the chick gets away with a rearender and an exchange of information. Of course she was balling and told the police that she was only going 3mph. I think she left a digit out. Anyway, guess I'll have start looking for parts. Don't know what her insurance will do. I told my son, if he's lucky they will total it and let him buy it back. Then I will fix it better than it was. <BR>  It's all just a big headache with the time and effort needed to get it back to norm. Thanks for allowing me to vent.<P>From this!!<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87GT4.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87GT3.jpg">  <P>To maybe....This  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ausconvertable.jpg"> <P>Peace, B2 OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 11-29-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000001||84Bill||11-29-2001||10:49 AM||||HER Insurence should cover the repairs||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||11-29-2001||12:10 PM||||Gezz.... Sorry to hear that BB... As long as he was all right....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P><BR>Looks like its time for a droptop...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlife.gif">    <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="purple">Goto Website - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||9
Z||000003||rogergarrison||11-29-2001||12:16 PM||||if she rear ended him and at a stop sign, shes got 2 counts against her already. Her insurance will have to pay. The cop was a jerk, he has no authority to estimate damage. Ive got bumped in a parking lot that was $3,000 damage. And he should have issued her a ticket for unassured clear distance at the very least. Maybe even failure to control her vehicle.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fformula88||11-29-2001||12:24 PM||||That really stinks!  Whether her insurance pays for it might depend on what they get told.  since the cop did not make out a report, it sounds like it is going to come down to her story vs yours.  Who knows what she will come up with!  <P>At least with that type of colission she is going to have trouble blaming it on your son.  However, insurance companies can be very stingy, and they may not want to pay all if they don't think she is "totally at fault"  <P>You should definately get an estimate on repairs from a body shop and get a good value of what the market value is on the car.  Both of these will be invaluable when dealing with her insurance company.  Also, do not accept their first offer since it will be low, and using your estimate and market value you should be able to get more cash out of them.  The market value is the important one for totalling the car!  Also, since its not your ins co, you shouldn't have to buy it back or any BS like that.  They should just cut you a check for the amount they are totalling it for(if it comes to that.  An 87 GT might not depending on how bad the frame is underneath!)<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/formulasig.JPG">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000005||BAM-BAM||11-29-2001||12:56 PM||||Thanks for the replies. Yeah, I thought that was kind of queer that she rearended him at a stop sign and got no ticket. I am having my son go over to the police station today and verify that ruling. He did however make them do an information exchange in his presence, what ever that's worth. The fact is that women can get away with anything if the smile enough or cry enough. It's just a sick fact of the justice system. I'm pissed now, this is gonna get hairy, I can just tell.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||84Bill||11-29-2001||01:00 PM||||No need to go to the station. If you have her insurance info just call her agent and report it to them. If they give you a hard time call your agent and tell them to handel it for you. <BR>About a month ago I was tagged on the right front fender, it scuffed the paint {buff job} and broke the signal lense {28 bucks fiero store} Guess what her insurance paid me..... 280 bucks!!! no questions asked||||reg||1
Z||000007||thomas_l||11-29-2001||01:25 PM||||Never mind a ticket. In your case the car in back pays, period. Do the following:<P>1. Go to a Pontiac dealer and two real good (expensive) body shops and get repair estimates - a total of three.<P>2. Write a letter (an old fashioned one using pen, paper, envelope and stamp) to her insurance company. The letter should include something like "although I have suffered some stiffness in my back & neck since the crash, I just want to be compensated for car repairs in the amount of $X ("low" estimate)."<P>3. Staple copies of the repair estimates to the letter and mail it off.<P>4. Don't stand too close to your mailbox because the insurance check will come in so fast it will probably knock it clean off its post  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I had a similar case (other guys fault but no ticket) and his insurance was dicking with me over salvage value. Needless to say I named my price and the threat of medical claims accelerated the process.<P>Good luck!||||reg||3
Z||000008||Fformula88||11-29-2001||02:49 PM||||Whatever works I suppose but I wouldn't throw in the medical expenses bit just yet.  First of all, most insurance companies are not going to be too intimidated by an "old fashioned letter"  They make their business screwing people out of money, and will definately not take you seriously.<P>Just file a claim with them.  They will investigate, ask their client what happened.  They will probably ask you for a statement too.  You do not have to give them one... they are not your ins. company... but since your not at fault and no injuries are involved there is no harm telling them what happened.  They will most likely want to see the car, although this depends on the company.  Then they will decide what to pay, and how much to pay based on their book values for parts and such.  I bet their estimate is about 33% less than a good body shops.  Thats where the dickering over value comes in.<P>Remember, on a small amount (like say $3000) they will not want to spend a lot of time dickering ver a few hundred bucks.  They will likely raise their offer a good amount and your gonna have to decide if its enough.<P>You should also let your ins company know someone rear-ended you.  This is different than putting in a claim!  If she decides to file a claim against you (some people are that crazy) at least your ins. company won't get blindsided.  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||11-29-2001||03:28 PM||||I wonder if going to Internal Affairs at the police department would accomplish anything. The woman driving the Explorer might have been "somebody's wife", if you know what I mean. Had a friend get screwed for his totaled Volvo, the same way. Maybe someone in the know would care to comment on this.<BR>I would absolutely tell your insurance company. Do you carry collision or comprehensive or uninsured motorist coverage? If so, let the insurance company fight this one for you.  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Sootah||11-29-2001||06:25 PM||||I actually pulled up next to your son at a stoplight about 3 weeks ago. Nice car, sorry to hear about that.<P>Oh, yeah, E-mail me BAM-BAM, I've lost your addie.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Nuclear_Happy_Face_Sig.jpg">        <BR><sup><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Black_Beauty_-_Front_Right.jpg" TARGET=_blank>The Black Beauty</A> (85 GT) - <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Busted-Ass_SE.jpg" TARGET=_blank>Bustedato</A> (86 SE, Parts car)<BR><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter<BR><B>MSN IM</B>: I_R_Sootah@hotmail.com<BR></sup>||||reg||1
Z||000011||BAM-BAM||11-30-2001||08:52 PM||||I guess Utah has some kind of modified no fault system. The claim has to be handled via your own insurance first, then after all is said and done, you can go after the other company, only if the amount exceeds a preset value. It's unlikely in this case that the amount will be excessive. Therefore my sons insurance will have to handle it and he will have to pay the penalties. Sounds like a load of crap to me. As for the ticket, well it seems that in Utah, or at least in the Cedar City jurisdiction, the officer can use personal discretion based on the "APPARENT" damages. That too sounds like a load of crap. Moral; Don't get hit in Cedar City Utah!!!!  <BR>  Hey, I want to thank all of you for the advice and well wishes. I love this place, you all know how to make a man feel better.<BR>  Oh, guess what I got to do today......I got to change the fuel pump in my 97 Suburban. WooHoo!!! What a load of fun. Hope none of you EVER have to do that.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||8
Z||000012||tgowens||11-30-2001||09:33 PM||||B-B, let me know what you need - I'll help you put it back together (that car is like one of my GT's!!! Great looking car!!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg"> <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000013||87GTZ34||12-01-2001||10:39 AM||||BB,<P>  So they have some 'modified' and subjective rules regarding accidents and property damage huh.  Well, if your son was hit that hard, he probably suffered some kind of injury to his neck, as the human body wasn't designed to go 0 to 30 in 0.1 seconds.  He should get looked at for by a doctor for subsequent symptoms and you/he should file from there.  The cop was obviously a rookie because if he was experienced/trained in accident investigations, he would know what kind of forces and acceleration are involved in that kind of accident and ticketed the girl to cover his own butt.  my .02  GL<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||BAM-BAM||12-01-2001||10:48 AM||||Finding out that in the town of Cedar City Utah, there are a lot of discretionary laws/habits. The officer was said to have acted within reason in his determination of weather the incident require a citation. That, paired with the modified no fault system, leaves my son and his insurance to pick up the tab. it's a messed up process.<BR>  Now, if it were another male driving the Ford Exploder, there would have been a citation, you can bet on that. But not for a cute, balling teenaged female. Like have always said, women and old people get away with murder.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||fropuff||12-01-2001||10:56 AM||||Sorry to hear that.  What a bunch of sh*t.  I don't really know what you're supposed to do.  If it were me, and Utah has a *good* justice system, I'd have your son sue that b*tch.  That way, the judge has to find fault for someone, and I'm pretty sure your son didn't do anything wrong; sitting at a stop and eveything.  I know suing doesn't really solve anything, but it kinda helps.  And have him get two expensive estimates, take the lower one, and sue her for that.  Then go around buying used parts.  At least then he wouldn't have to pay for the accident that wasn't his fault for the next few years on his insurance.  That really is a crappy situtation.  Hope everything goes okay for you guys.||||reg||1
